* Central Service

** Entities

*** Vendor (`/api/v1/vendors`)

**** Fields
     - id
     - firstName
     - lastName
     - email (unique)

**** Relationships
     - OneToMany printers → Printer
     - OneToMany printTransactions → PrintTransaction

*** Printer (`/api/v1/printers`)

**** Fields
     - id
     - name
     - capabilities

**** Relationships
     - ManyToOne vendor → Vendor
     - OneToMany printTransactions → PrintTransaction

*** PrintTransaction (`/api/v1/transactions`)

**** Fields
     - id

**** Relationships
     - ManyToOne vendor → Vendor
     - ManyToOne printer → Printer (nullable)
     - OneToMany documents → Document

*** Document (`/api/v1/documents`)
**** Fields
     - id
     - name
     - path
     - status
     - configuration (nullable, length *0)
**** Relationships
     - ManyToOne printTransaction → PrintTransaction

*** Relationships

    @code mermaid
    erDiagram
    Vendor ||--o{ Printer  has
    Vendor ||--o{ PrintTransaction  initiates
    Printer ||--o{ PrintTransaction  handles
    PrintTransaction ||--o{ Document  contains
    @end

** Server WebSocket Namespaces (Socket.IO)

*** Single Notification Namespace (`/notifications`)

**** (`join_vendor`)

     The vendor application when starts, emits this event to the server, the server puts him into a private room identified by this vendor's id.

     @code json
     {
       "id" : 123 // vendor id
     }
     @end

     - Should occur when the desktop application starts-up (restarts).

**** (`new_transaction`)

     When the server receives a new transaction using REST to this vendor, it emits an event specifically to the vendor's private room.

     @code json
     {
       "id": 123 // transaction id
     }
     @end

     The vendor application can then request the transaction content with this `id` using a REST endpoint.

     - Should occur when a new transaction is made from the mobile frontend from the REST endpoint.

**** (`join_transaction`)

     The customer's browser will emit this event after creating a new transaction, the server will put him in a private room identified by transaction's id.

     @code json
     {
       "id" : 123 // transaction id
     }
     @end

     - Should occur immediately after the vendor approves the transaction.

**** (`update_progress`)

     Now when the desktop application updates the transaction status, the server emits this event specifically to the creator of this transaction (to the room identified by this transaction).

     @code json
     {
       "id": 123 // transaction id
       "progress": "printing" // progress status
     }
     @end

     - Should occur when there is an update on the status of the transaction.
